    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d246">

                <pb facs="0410" n="286" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg286"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/179b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Uruguay</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Jeffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-02-05T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">5 February,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3. We would like Minister Buero<anchor n="7" xml:id="d246-f1"/> to be informed
                    that this Government proposes recognizing the Bolivian Government as the
                    Constitutional Government of that Republic and the opportunity thus afforded
                    Uruguay to extend recognition at the same time, if that course accords with its
                    own policy. Formal recognition will be extended by the American Minister at La
                    Paz on February 9. It is our understanding that Argentina, Brazil and Chile will
                    accord recognition on that date also.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d246-f1" n="7" xml:id="d246-f1-content">
                <p>Juan Antonio Buero, Uruguayan Minister of Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
